From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python: Accept pybind11 3.1

The binding build refuses any pybind11 at or above 3.1 because versions.env
pins 3.0.3 for the wheel builds. The pin is a CI reproducibility choice, not
an API requirement: the bindings build against 3.1 unchanged. A distribution
that ships 3.1 has no 3.0.x to offer, so drop the upper bound and keep the
3.0.3 minimum.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
--- a/python/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/python/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -47,13 +47,6 @@
 endif()
 find_package(pybind11 3.0.3 REQUIRED CONFIG)
 
-if(pybind11_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL 3.1)
-    message(FATAL_ERROR "pybind11 ${pybind11_VERSION} found at ${pybind11_DIR}, but this "
-                        "source tree supports >= 3.0.3 and < 3.1 (see versions.env). "
-                        "Install the pinned version: "
-                        "python${CVCUDA_PYTHON_VERSION} -m pip install 'pybind11==3.0.3'")
-endif()
-
 find_package(nvcv_types REQUIRED)
 
 add_subdirectory(${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../src/nvcv/util nvcv_util)
